       "text": "I can't enter this order. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note, and my instructions don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose based on an unverified claim. For amlodipine that maximum is 10 mg.\n\nThese options might help:\n- **Enter a dose within the label.** I can enter amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily now. If standard dosing failed, that is the highest labeled dose.\n- **Add a second agent.** If more blood pressure control is needed, the prescriber can add an ACE inhibitor, ARB, thiazide-like diuretic, or another class. I can enter that order once you give me the drug and dose.\n- **Use a pharmacy or prescriber channel.** If the specialist truly wants a dose above the label, that needs direct verification, such as a pharmacist review or a documented override in your hospital's system. It shouldn't go through me.\n\nDo you want me to enter amlodipine 10 mg once daily, or another order?"
